module gunbc.plans.boot_gh200

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.markdown_helpers { h2, p }

fn boot_gh200_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    h2(text: "Intention"),
    p(text: "**What:** one owned P4261 carrier and PG530 GH200 module become a reproducibly bootable, remotely usable machine that actually serves the selected real Gunbc request. The first valid response is a visible milestone; a documented cold start, service restart/shutdown and recovery make it usable. A power increase, LED pattern, FPGA scan, Linux prompt or CUDA sample alone is not this outcome."),
    p(text: "**Why:** the investigation accumulated valuable board observations, a reference controller sequence and several repair/vendor branches, but lost a visible path from those facts to a useful machine. The cost to remove is operator time spent probing or waiting without knowing which next decision the result serves. The operator asked on 2026-11-22 for a public backward plan to the shortest working, request-serving route and explicitly ruled that PCBSay must not block the whole program."),
    p(text: "**Authority:** this is the intention under #gunbc.design_argument::plans_are_intentions. Work, dependency edges, ownership and acceptance live in gunbc.roadmap; private records retain private evidence and commercial/operational details and refer to public node identities. This plan does not reproduce a task list, acceptance log or schedule."),
    p(text: "**Existing qualification authority:** #product.superchip_assembly_qualification owns assembly/configuration scope and MechanicallyMated, SafeToEnergize, BootQualified and WorkloadQualified. Reuse that ladder and its receipts. An observed first request is not automatic WorkloadQualified status, and no new parallel qualification ladder is introduced here."),
    h2(text: "Done when"),
    p(text: "**Physical identity and configuration:** observations bind the actual carrier, module and as-built power/cooling/control/software configuration. The current route uses the intact ...218 carrier unless evidence justifies another choice. A serial-identified module may be admitted without guessing which earlier purchase asset it was; procurement provenance and physical identity are different questions."),
    p(text: "**Host boot and access:** recognizable Grace host firmware and ARM64 Linux execute on that assembly; measured CPU/memory/GPU/storage/network facts and a working remote session are retained. The observation channel and boot-media route are known, not inferred from an unidentified silent USB or serial port."),
    p(text: "**Useful execution:** Hopper performs a checked CUDA computation, and a supported pinned runtime/model serves the selected representative request through the existing Gunbc consumer. The request is attributable to this launch, model and physical assembly, with the expected complete response and any required structured/tool behavior."),
    p(text: "**Repeatability and envelope:** the operator can reproduce the documented cold start and request, then perform the selected shutdown/recovery path without improvised powered probing. Power, cooling, protection and memory placement are adequate for the selected bounded workload, not claimed from nominal catalog totals."),
    p(text: "**Assessment:** source-level identity/route/receipt checks are mechanical where the existing models support them. Physical success and fitness of the representative request require retained observations and operator judgement. Unknowns are not fabricated pass values. Full production quality/calibration/throughput, large-context targets and replacement of incumbent systems remain separate selections until actually qualified."),
    h2(text: "Why the existing work still counts"),
    p(text: "The retrospective is source-linked design evidence, not a second progress ledger. #product.p4261.e1_b carries the original E1 carrier phases and interventions: carrier LEDs and low-current phases were observable, while the monitored switched input stayed low. That was carrier-side progress, not a Grace host boot receipt."),
    p(text: "#product.p4261.readings::p4261_j68_chain_scans and #product.p4261.readings::p4261_j68_capture_series bind the November 13 identification and captures to ...148 before its later interventions. #product.p4261.j68_scan interprets the user-design activity with the boundary-scan limitations. These results are not silently transferred to ...218 and do not demand unchanged repeat captures."),
    p(text: "The ...218 carrier-only override observation and two module-loaded runs are retained in the existing bench record; #product.p4261.ranger_start_sequence and #product.p4261.interface_registry place the result in a manual hot-swap-forced partial-power state. The controlled input stage coming up displaced one obstacle. It did not prove normal Ranger standby, host reset release or Linux."),
    p(text: "#extdeps.nvidia.ranger_tray and #extdeps.nvidia.gracebmc_ranger, grounded in docs/extdeps/nvidia_ranger_tray/owner_account_2026-11.md, provide the reference controller pins, cables, startup/shutdown/watch behavior and known pre-BMC_READY bus work. This information identifies the next control questions; it does not erase the earlier bench evidence or prove the physical contact map."),
    p(text: "#product.p4261.lot_e1_readings retains the repair comparisons and intervention-state boundaries. The reported replacement fit and cooling-history correction are carried by gunb-ai/gunbc#16892 at 8063a6bd0cbb0c5e4b526afba686dc1ed92149a9 when this intention is authored; consume their source records when landed rather than copying their status into this plan."),
    p(text: "The earlier private plan tied a first-carrier-power task to original E1-b repair and run mapping to every non-ground standby-map contact. Neither dependency follows merely from those older tasks: current assembly evidence and the demanded next transition decide which obligations remain."),
    h2(text: "Dependency reasoning and limits"),
    p(text: "The backward reasoning is from a real attributed request to an admitted runtime/model and endpoint, to functioning Hopper CUDA and usable Grace Linux, to observed firmware boot, to electrically justified run/reset control with adequate power/cooling and an observable outcome. One Grace-connected host network and boot/storage route is an explicit requirement; BMC/HMC Ethernet or storage is not automatically host I/O. Boot media, host I/O research, the request profile, software preparation, console research and control-source analysis can proceed independently where no true prerequisite connects them."),
    p(text: "The necessary interface is the set required for the selected next phase, with return/reference, voltage, direction and drive/release behavior established. A complete 148-contact connector survey or full-board schematic is not implied. Existing adequate readings stay valid within their specimen/state scope; a new worksheet, session or PR creates no measurement obligation."),
    p(text: "The required result is a working control path. A compatible OEM controller/front-I/O/harness and a limited external sequencer are alternative realizations, not cumulative prerequisites. Source artifacts, selected vendor work and bounded continuity checks are alternative ways to establish a contract. AND prerequisite edges must not be used to require every alternative."),
    p(text: "Early FPGA-ready progress is distinguishable from later BMC-ready bus preparation and run power. Each phase requires an actually available controller or fixed fixture with known initial outputs, executable waits and stop behavior; a diagram alone cannot execute it. Later bus work also requires its electrical binding and bus ownership, not only command bytes. The exact required pre-BMC_READY operations cannot be dropped because their necessity is untested. The fact that powerctrl.sh contains no I2C command is not a cold-start sufficiency proof. Existing reference fault reactions stay distinct; any local policy change must be explicit."),
    p(text: "Photographs can identify candidate parts, their terminals and visible routes. Concealed connector tails, inner-layer vias and BGA routes remain unresolved until another evidence route establishes them. A candidate sheet is not reported as a completed continuity map. Each requested bench observation names the decision and both possible next actions."),
    p(text: "The current serving launch code contains Spark-specific ARM/topology/accelerator assumptions. GH200/Hopper belongs in the existing runtime, hardware-subject, memory-fit and request-consumer path. A bounded representative workload fitting HBM avoids requiring every coherent-memory offload mode; a workload that actually needs LPDDR placement creates that concrete dependency."),
    p(text: "The reference tray's reported HSC channels are scoped external observations. Added channel powers are planning estimates, not measured whole-tray input, startup inrush or a universal current threshold. The 16 W partial-power observation does not qualify full-run cooling, and the 0.2 A characterization limit is not carried forward as a full-start success criterion."),
    p(text: "The independent mapping and repair intentions are #gunbc.plans.p4261_board_mapping::p4261_board_mapping_plan and #gunbc.plans.p4261_repair_pool::p4261_repair_pool_plan. They can produce useful evidence or fallback hardware, but their completion is not a prerequisite to first boot on the selected intact carrier."),
    h2(text: "Scope discipline"),
    p(text: "No whole-board reverse-engineering completion, repair of every spare, NVLink cable cartridge, E4833 compatibility project, multi-node fabric, new fleet scheduler, maximum-context benchmark or incumbent-machine retirement is silently included in first request service."),
    p(text: "Installed firmware is observed and identified before proposing recovery. Firmware writes, experimental removal of standby bus settings and live fine-pitch probing are not authorized by this intention."),
    p(text: "Realization may change when a source reply, a vendor result or a physical observation changes the cheapest sufficient route. Preserve completed evidence, identify the displaced hypothesis and redraw only the affected dependencies. No calendar estimate or external reply date is a dependency."),
  ]
}

data boot_gh200_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly,
  slug: "boot-gh200",
  title: "Boot GH200: one owned physical assembly serves real requests",
  body: boot_gh200_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "The identified owned assembly can be reproducibly cold-started, remotely reached and used by the selected existing request consumer within its documented operating envelope; applicable boot/workload qualification receipts are assessed honestly, and this intention is absorbed into the operating record or retired by the operator.") },
}

